  <section|Important checks and remaining
  boundaries><label|important-checks-and-remaining-boundaries>

  The rescaling direction is lambda=g(beta)/g(beta'), so
  g(beta')lambda=g(beta). Full Gaussian coordinates and the same covariance
  are retained when comparing parameters. The Gaussian moment bounds alone
  were insufficient for a pointwise common dominator; the manuscript
  explicitly adds the uniform exp(z^TQz/8) envelope. The anchored
  compensation exponent vanishes at the base point, avoiding an unsupported
  exponential-polynomial moment assumption.

  The perturbed cluster support factor is exp((a+delta)c(Y)), exactly as in
  Elixir.comforts. Its root price changes from gamma to 3gamma/2, and its
  ratio from 1/2 to 3/4. The comparison radius may depend on the fixed torus.
  Common representation, dictionaries, path, clipping, masks, rooms, incoming
  activities and projected-covariance premises remain explicit.

  Read-only source inspection used <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|sed> and
  <verbatim|cat>. No Lean commands, axiom replay, or source edits were
  performed. TeX and structural checks belong in <verbatim|validation.md>; no
  agent pass is converted into a human approval or reviewed unit status.

